Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:55:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(parser): read "haven't added mana with this ability
 this turn"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unlocks Carpet of Flowers, one of the two cards the Paradox Power precon
reported as unsupported.

The condition is the NEGATIVE reading of the per-ability resolution tally that
`AbilityUseCountThisTurn` already carries, so it needs a third template arm and
no engine change at all: `{ tally: Resolved, comparator: LT, n: 1 }`. `LT 1`
rather than `EQ 0` because `n` is a `u32` on the variant and zero is not in the
comparison vocabulary its siblings use.

Checked the `add-engine-variant` gate first, and it returned
REFUSE_WITH_EXISTING_SLOT: `AbilityUseCountThisTurn` keys by
`(source_id, ability_index)` and is cleared at end of turn, which is exactly
"this ability, this turn". A "produced mana" tally would need `ManaAdded` to
carry an `ability_index` — it carries only `source_id`, so mana cannot be
attributed to a printed ability at all — and the gap it would close is empty
here: the ability requires a target opponent and adds X mana where X is that
opponent's Island count, so a resolution that occurs always adds mana.

Result: WHO unsupported cards 26 -> 25; Paradox Power precon 2 -> 1.
